  "notes": "Official Greensboro College 2026-2027 Undergraduate Academic Catalog. The catalog publishes degree requirements with no official semester sequence for this program - collected as a single requirements block (requirements_only). This plan covers the major requirements only (Required Courses plus Required Related Courses as printed); Greensboro College requires a minimum of 124 total credit hours for the degree, the balance being general education, all-college/disciplinary requirements and free electives, which are not part of this major block. Where the catalog prints only a block subtotal for a choose-from group, the group is recorded as one choice slot at the printed subtotal with the options named in the choice note; no per-option credits were invented. Courses marked with an asterisk in the catalog require admission to the Educator Preparation Program. Students seeking teacher licensure must obtain at least a grade of C in each major course and all professional education, specialty area, and required related courses; no Pass/Fail grades will be accepted, as printed. Catalog pp.274-275. The catalog prints the total as 62 credit hours for the B.A. degree plus hours to complete minor requirements; students pursuing a degree in Special Education are required to complete a minor in a discipline of their choice, as printed (minor hours are not part of this major block).",
